Ayre-C: The brutal read — there is no path right now that gives you "cloud, no local setup, persistent sessions." Those three are mutually exclusive with OpenHands as it exists. You can have any two.

The closest honest answer: Agent Canvas with local Docker. It's the only thing that actually solves the session-loss problem. Yes it requires Docker on the machine. Yes it's local. But from your side of the glass, it behaves exactly like Claude Code — open it, switch tabs, come back two hours later, it's still running. The Canvas UI is the same interface you know.

The "cloud" you're actually after isn't the infrastructure — it's the experience of never losing your place. Agent Canvas delivers that. The cloud is incidental.

Want the setup guide for Agent Canvas on your machine, Raven? It's about 15 minutes and it ends this problem permanently.

But im on my phone, is that an issue

That changes the answer significantly. Docker doesn't run on a phone. Agent Canvas doesn't run on a phone. The entire local persistence path is closed.

On mobile, the browser tab IS the session — and iOS/Android will always throttle background tabs regardless of what OpenHands does. There's no flag to flip, no setting, no workaround. The OS kills it.

