The architecture needs to be:

.openhands/task_tracker.json — session working copy, written by sl.py, not committed
audit/starlogs/ — committed StarLogs, the permanent record (git = source of truth)
sl.py — the tool that syncs both
Flow:

On session START: sl.py reads last StarLog, writes .openhands/task_tracker.json
On task change: sl.py writes .openhands/task_tracker.json AND the last StarLog gets updated (or a new StarLog entry made)
On session CLOSE: sl.py --commit reads from tracker, writes final StarLog, commits both tracker + StarLog
The OpenHands task_tracker tool reads/writes .openhands/task_tracker.json — it stays in sync with sl.py.

This means:

StarLogs are always committed (they go to git)
The tracker file is a working copy, never committed (it's in .gitignore or not added)
Cross-session persistence comes from the last committed StarLog
