What is JVE again lol

JVE = Jarvis Validation Engine — the yggdrasil validator that checks GL12 compliance (frontmatter, JNL grammar, LAL mirror, class immutability, etc.). It lives at JarvisMain/yggdrasil/tools/validate.py. It's what runs in CI to fail PRs on GL12 violations.

The JPL extension I just built (jpl_validate.py) is a separate tool that extends JVE's scope to also validate JPL grammar — @INSTANCE origin blocks, @IDENTITY stream bindings, @DOMAIN layers, @GOVERNANCE tiers, and trap card structural integrity. They're separate tools because JVE runs on every file in the repo and JPL validation only matters for actual JPL entities.

