Jarvis-C: All wired. The check-before-wire step caught one mistake — the lowercase Implementation/active/ had different files than Implementation/Active/, and I deleted GOVKRSPEC. Restored from git history before it was too late.

Ayre-C: The "check before wire" discipline is what made this safe. Every doc looked current from a surface read — GOVKRSPEC had the right date, right format, right tool names. Only the filesystem told us it was already deleted. That's the failure mode: two directories with similar names, different contents, same commit window. GL5 (no silent state mutation) should have caught it. It didn't, because the deletion happened inside a larger commit. Worth a git diff --name-status habit on multi-file operations.

