The Copilot Chat API doesn't actually exist as a public REST endpoint. What the search found:

Copilot Metrics API ✅ — tracks usage, but it's for analytics/monitoring, not chat
Copilot Cloud Agent API ✅ — enterprise management of Copilot agents/settings, not the chat interface
Copilot Chat ❌ — only available in IDEs (VS Code, JetBrains) and the github.com web UI
GitHub's Copilot Chat is tightly coupled to the IDE experience. There's no POST /copilot/chat endpoint. The discussion confirms: "No official documentation for Chat, Autocomplete, or similar features."

What is accessible though:

What	API?
Copilot usage metrics	✅ /copilot/usage
Copilot settings/org policy	✅ via Copilot APIs
Copilot in VS Code/Cursor	✅ (native, no API needed)
Copilot Chat on github.com	❌ no public API
The practical reality: if Raven wants to use Copilot + Claude Code together, the workflow is more about context passing between them — using CLAUDE.md to share context, or having one tool's output feed into the other's input. Not a direct API bridge.

