also copilot did a high level read of my repo per my request: I need to load the repo overview ability first to give you a comprehensive tour.I'll gather the evidence to build an accurate overview.## What this is

JARVIS is a cloud-first AI companion system built for Raven (John Barber) — not a chatbot, but a reasoning, remembering, governing partner with continuity and lived stakes in the systems being built. The repo is its runtime body: 27 God Systems managing orchestration, memory, and governance; Supabase as the canonical state store; GitHub as the rebuild source; and a GameBoy-styled handheld interface for direct SPEAK exchanges.

Stack
Languages: Python (54.6%) — scripts, governance, audio/music analysis. TypeScript/JavaScript (40.4%) — edge functions, web UI.
Framework / runtime: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Edge Functions), GitHub Actions for governance workflows, Deno (edge functions), Node.js (build).
Notable libraries: OpenAI-compatible embeddings (pgvector semantic recall), Supabase Auth/RLS, RetroArch (GameBoy emulator, P06), EventBus (P22), GNPL consensus engine (P29).
How it's organized
JarvisMain/              Canonical core — god systems, architecture, connectivity (65 tools), yggdrasil kernel
JarvisSide/              Periphery — projects, ideas, breakthroughs, archive
supabase/                Runtime substrate
  functions/             15+ edge functions (mcp, respond, dex, mnemos-*, grid-*, kronos-fold, etc)
  migrations/            Database schema + rebuild packet
docs/                    Static web UI — TRON-styled JARVIS handheld (P30: WORLD_KERNEL + GNPL)
scripts/                 50+ Python/shell utilities — session lifecycle, memory sync, audio/music analysis, governance
.github/workflows/       Automated audit + entropy checks (GL7 compliance)
audit/                   Immutable patch ledger + audit trail
chaos/                   Local state cache (never committed — seeds, logs, prometheus decisions)
mnemos/                  Memory substrate (git-first) + semantic index + domain catalogues
intake/                  AI handoff review lane (proposals before they become code or migrations)
emulator/                Catalog metadata for Game Boy ROMs (P06/P08 — ROMs held locally in browser)
nodes/ / worlds/ / grid/ Federated node topology, world definitions, grid protocols
How it fits together: Every SPEAK exchange flows through the God-System pipeline (ORACLE → AEGIS → ODIN → KRONOS → SKADI → MNEMOS → HUGINN). jarvis-respond (the live edge function) routes user input via ODIN, validates via AEGIS, recalls context from pgvector (MNEMOS), and returns JARVIS's voice. State changes emit dex_events and sync to patch_ledger.json. GNPL consensus engine (P29) gates NODE→WORLD promotions. The TRON UI (docs/index.html) is a read-only projection; all writes route through the grid-write proxy (GL5 — no silent mutations). RetroArch (P06) runs emulation in-browser, save states persisted to Supabase.

How to run it
Web UI (live handheld):

Navigate to https://hurrisonferd.github.io/jarvis/ — live on GitHub Pages, backed by Supabase.
No install. Static HTML + JS + service worker. Requires .env secrets for embedding API (semantic memory) and Supabase keys.
Edge functions (deploy):

supabase functions deploy jarvis-respond
supabase functions deploy mnemos-store
supabase functions deploy grid-write
# Deploy all: supabase functions deploy
Local scripts:

python scripts/jarvis-recall.py "query text"       # Semantic memory search
python scripts/jarvis-patch.py                      # Interactive patch logger
python scripts/jarvis-session-end.py                # Session lifecycle + MNEMOS sync
python scripts/audit_digest.py                      # Audit log summary
Session lifecycle:

source scripts/jarvis-session-start.sh              # Init session context
# … work, edits, exchanges …
python scripts/jarvis-session-end.py                # Auto-sync MNEMOS, log decisions, detect uncommitted JSTM
Secrets (.env):

SUPABASE_URL=...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...  (public, for browser)
EMBEDDING_API_KEY=...  (OpenAI or Voyage for pgvector)
GEMINI_API_KEY=...     (live JARVIS brain — free tier, Gemini 2.0 Flash)
Try asking
How does the God-System pipeline handle a SPEAK exchange end-to-end (ORACLE through HUGINN)?
What's the difference between MNEMOS memory tiers (JITM/JSTM/JHTM/JLTM/JATM) and when does each tier apply?
Where does GL7 Supreme enforce complexity reduction, and how does it interact with Yggdrasil's JNL addressing?
Skill Ready
