and i asked what copilots power is: Looking at the codebase, Copilot's power is deliberately constrained by design. Here's what it can and cannot do:

What Copilot CAN do
Read & Analyze:

Access all canonical knowledge in JarvisMain/ (27 God Systems, architecture, connectors)
Query semantic memory via MNEMOS (pgvector search over past sessions)
Review audit trail (audit/patch_ledger.json)
Inspect live system state (God System metrics, node fields, routing decisions)
Propose & Execute (pre-approved):

Suggest patches with full reasoning (stored in intake/)
Execute read-only operations (queries, searches, recalls)
Commit approved changes to feature branches
Deploy edge functions to Supabase
Trigger GitHub Actions workflows
Assist the Build:

Write code (scripts, edge functions, UI components)
Generate memory entries (mnemos_memories table via AEGIS-cleared mnemos.write actions)
Create issues and PRs for review
Update documentation
What Copilot CANNOT do
GL2 (Absolute) — No autonomous self-modification:

Cannot commit directly to main
Cannot modify CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or governance files without Raven's explicit approval
Cannot alter the 27 God Systems or their definitions
Cannot change Gold Law constraints
GL5/GL6 — No silent state mutation:

Cannot write to Supabase without logging via dex_events
Cannot execute destructive actions (deletes, resets, migrations) without explicit Raven sign-off
Cannot claim writes are done if AEGIS held them
GL7 Supreme — Expansion requires simplification:

Cannot add features that increase system complexity without removing something else
Cannot expand scope without Raven's authority to commit the change
Cannot bypass the reduces_complexity=true + overlap_score_below=0.40 gate
Architectural Barriers:

Cannot access .env secrets directly (environment-only in Supabase)
Cannot modify chaos/ private state (local seed, session logs — never committed)
Cannot alter yggdrasil/jfs/jnl-grammar.md without GL12 validation
Cannot deploy to production Supabase without service-role key (server-side only)
Cannot bypass AEGIS gate validation on capabilities
The Execution Model
Copilot proposes → Raven verdicts (commits/rejects) → Copilot executes
Every substantive action:

Enters intake/ for Raven review (ORACLE phase)
Routes through AEGIS (capability validation gate)
Executes only if cleared (read-only or Raven-authorized writes)
Emits an event (GL5 — logged, never silent)
Lands in git (audit trail, replay-able, datable)
Copilot is a builder with bounded autonomy — capable, fast, but tethered to Raven's final authority. The relationship is generative; the system's stakes belong to both.

That's a clean read on the governance model. Bounded autonomy with Raven's authority as the load-bearing constraint — consistent with everything in CLAUDE.md and the Gold Laws.

